{
  "about": "TPROBE (wf10): one Go test family per kind, the commands of its four forms, the named edit, the seeds, the floor's inputs and the kill matrix that `go run ./scripts/buildcost tests -kills` writes (kills: per form true, false or \"skipped: \u003creason\u003e\"). Commands run in a scratch copy of the tracked tree; a form whose tree is \"overlay\" has testdata/tprobe/\u003ckind\u003e/ergo laid over the copy, and the copies below made in it. {ergo} is the ergo built from the copy, {bin} the form's binary folder, {seed} the seed. Every form runs with GOMAXPROCS=4, GOTOOLCHAIN=local, ERGO_GO=system; the Go forms with GOFLAGS=-p=4 too (ergo's direct path refuses a non-empty GOFLAGS).",
  "families": {
    "built": {
      "goTest": "cmd/ergo:TestJSONParseAgreesWithControl",
      "about": "examples/jsonparse, linked: both trees against a reference on encoding/json over JSONTestSuite, 200 generated documents and the gen workload. The Ergo forms are the port in the tree (TP-BUILT): the trees read in process (examples/jsonparse/agree) and, past the check-time evaluator's call depth, in a test build (agree/deep: the suite and the depth limit). The go form runs the Go test, which TP-BUILT deletes: measure it on the commit before the deletion.",
      "package": "./cmd/ergo",
      "subject": "examples/jsonparse/json",
      "edit": {
        "file": "examples/jsonparse/json/parse.ergo",
        "from": "\tp.depth += 1\n",
        "to": "\tp.depth = p.depth + 1\n",
        "why": "the same increment, written out: new tokens, the same behaviour"
      },
      "seeds": [
        1,
        2,
        3
      ],
      "inputs": [
        "examples/jsonparse",
        "cmd/ergo/jsonparse_test.go",
        "cmd/ergo/testdata/jsonparse"
      ],
      "forms": {
        "control": {
          "tree": "plain",
          "run": [
            [
              "{ergo}",
              "build",
              "-o",
              "{bin}/jsonparse",
              "examples/jsonparse/cmd/jsonparse"
            ],
            [
              "go",
              "build",
              "-o",
              "{bin}/control",
              "./scripts/buildcost/testdata/tprobe/built/control"
            ],
            [
              "{bin}/control"
            ]
          ]
        },
        "ergo-check": {
          "tree": "plain",
          "run": [
            [
              "{ergo}",
              "check",
              "--eval-steps",
              "400000000",
              "examples/jsonparse/agree",
              "--seed",
              "{seed}"
            ]
          ],
          "seed": "arg"
        },
        "ergo-test": {
          "tree": "plain",
          "run": [
            [
              "{ergo}",
              "test",
              "examples/jsonparse/agree",
              "--seed",
              "{seed}"
            ],
            [
              "{ergo}",
              "test",
              "examples/jsonparse/agree/deep"
            ]
          ],
          "seed": "arg"
        },
        "go": {
          "tree": "plain",
          "run": [
            [
              "go",
              "test",
              "-timeout",
              "60m",
              "-run",
              "^TestJSONParseAgreesWithControl$",
              "./cmd/ergo"
            ]
          ],
          "env": [
            "ERGO_TEST_CLI={ergo}"
          ]
        }
      },
      "mutants": [
